        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-bootstrap-llm"
        },
        "markdown": "## Use the current instructions\n\nThe **Copy bootstrap handshake** button beside Twilite’s address bar supplies the starting prompt.\n\nAsk your AI to read:\n\n- [Twilite onboarding](https://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/onboarding.md)\n- [Current node composition](https://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/nodes/graph-native-node-composition.md)\n\nIf it cannot open those documents, provide their text before continuing.\n\nThe first reply should be one small additive JSON transaction. Copy the JSON and paste it into your new graph. Check the result before requesting more.\n\nFor your saved graph, ask for the current declaration, its views, glyph, and landing surface. Content belongs in Content nodes. A named Port is needed only when you want to expose an additional connection endpoint.\n",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1783087308631,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
