      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-bootstrap-llm"
        },
        "markdown": "## Give your work a starting shape\n\nAfter the handshake, copy this prompt into your AI chat:\n\n```text\nHelp me plan a small workshop in Twilite.\nFollow the current Graph-Native Node Composition contract.\nCreate a small graph with a question, venue notes, a decision,\nand a next step. Label the relationships so I can follow the\nreasoning. Use clearly marked fictional notes for this example.\nInclude the declaration, default/summary/icon views, glyph,\nand landing surface required by the current contract.\nUse Content nodes for the material. Do not add a separate root\nPort. Return one additive JSON transaction for my new graph.\n```\n\nReplace the workshop with your own topic when you are ready.\n\n### Keep what you made\n\nTrying authoring is free; saving requires production access. Open **Document actions → Unlock production tools** for account options. Once saving is enabled, use **Save As… → Save to GitHub** or **Save locally**. Reopen the saved graph and check it before closing your work.\n",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1783087305719,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
